  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a large jump over config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is highly beneficial. Image-only (config_010, 0.208) is far weaker, so the RNA pathway is the primary signal. Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether transformer aggregation can outperform simple avgpool for multiprofile RNA. This experiment (config_003) isolates that single variable—aggregation method—while holding model_setting, profile_setting, and encoder constant, making it a clean A/B comparison against config_002. If transformer helps, it validates a more expressive aggregation strategy that would benefit all downstream multimodal configurations; if it does not, we can confidently default to avgpool and redirect budget toward encoder or fusion choices. Under a limited budget, resolving this foundational design question before exploring encoders or multimodal fusion is the most information-efficient next step."
